    "background_story": "Ellis was a brilliant and eccentric archaeologist with a passion for glyptography, the study of ancient seals and gemstones. Growing up in a family of collectors, he was fascinated by the intricate carvings on his grandfather's antique signet rings. Ellis spent years honing his skills, becoming an expert in deciphering the symbols and stories etched into these tiny works of art. His groundbreaking research on the glyptics of ancient Mesopotamia led to a major discovery: a previously unknown seal of a Sumerian king. The find sparked a new wave of interest in glyptography, and Ellis was hailed as a pioneer in his field. He continued to uncover the secrets of these ancient stones, revealing the stories of civilizations long forgotten.",
